{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.DecayFibreBarParity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayFibreBarParity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DecayFibreBarParity.cap_member_of_family","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayFibreBarParity.cap_member_of_family","kind":"theorem","line":252,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayFibreBarParity.lean#L252-L259","doc":"**The `y_(1³) = 0` member of that family**, exhibited: the cap is a choice\nof representative, not a consequence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DecayFibreBarParity.threeRow_undetermined_by_decay","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayFibreBarParity.threeRow_undetermined_by_decay","kind":"theorem","line":240,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayFibreBarParity.lean#L240-L250","doc":"**The decay channel cannot determine the three-row weight.** For ANY\nprescribed value `t` of `y_(1³)`, there is a normalised weight triple whose\ndecay pairing is the given `g`. The cap picks one member of this family; the\ndata cannot. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DecayFibreBarParity.fullBar_add_const","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayFibreBarParity.fullBar_add_const","kind":"theorem","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayFibreBarParity.lean#L218-L222","doc":"**Every constant is bar-even**, hence `z_D + c` is full-bar whenever `z_D`\nis. Together with `fullBar_add_barEven` this is the precise sense in which\nbar-parity cannot constrain the value at a point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DecayFibreBarParity.y21_at_augmentation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayFibreBarParity.y21_at_augmentation","kind":"theorem","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayFibreBarParity.lean#L210-L216","doc":"**The augmentation is NOT faithful:** `y_(2,1)(q) = 0` exactly. This is what\npicks `z_D` out of the admissible pair `{q, z_D}` — and it is structural, being\nthe corpus's own `hfaith` hypothesis, rather than a further ruling. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DecayFibreBarParity.y21","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayFibreBarParity.y21","kind":"def","line":206,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayFibreBarParity.lean#L206-L208","doc":"The `(2,1)` Ocneanu weight, as a function of `q` and the Markov parameter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DecayFibreBarParity.fullBar_add_barEven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayFibreBarParity.fullBar_add_barEven","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayFibreBarParity.lean#L172-L179","doc":"**The full-bar family is affine over the bar-even functions**, so bar-parity\nnarrows the fibre without pinning a unique `z`. If `z` is full-bar and `f` is\nbar-even, then `z + f` is full-bar too. `z = q` and `z_D` are both in the\nfamily. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DecayFibreBarParity.barEven_not_fullBar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayFibreBarParity.barEven_not_fullBar","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayFibreBarParity.lean#L162-L168","doc":"**A bar-EVEN parameter is never full-bar** away from `q = 1`. `z_C` is\nbar-even, which is why the C-frame ladder cannot carry a bar-odd decay trace —\nthe content of `decayLadder_zC_threeRow_ne_zero`, seen from the parity side. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DecayFibreBarParity.one_not_fullBar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayFibreBarParity.one_not_fullBar","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayFibreBarParity.lean#L154-L160","doc":"**`z = 1` is NOT full-bar** (for `h ≠ 0`, i.e. away from `q = 1`). The\ncoordinate-sum point is bar-EVEN — `bar(1) = 1` — and bar-even is a DIFFERENT\ncondition from full-bar. This is the second, cap-free exclusion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DecayFibreBarParity.decayTrace_bar_odd_of_fullBar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayFibreBarParity.decayTrace_bar_odd_of_fullBar","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayFibreBarParity.lean#L136-L145","doc":"**THE FIBRE CONSTRAINT.** When `z` satisfies the full-bar condition, the\ndecay trace `g(z)·χ^(3)(Δ_S)` is bar-ODD.\n\nThis is the half that does the work: it holds with no appeal to `y_(1³) = 0`,\nso it is independent of the two-row cap and hence of the owner ruling that\nimported the cap into this channel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DecayFibreBarParity.g_bar_even_iff_fullBar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayFibreBarParity.g_bar_even_iff_fullBar","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayFibreBarParity.lean#L102-L127","doc":"**The carrier scalar is bar-EVEN exactly on the full-bar condition.**\n`g` at `(q⁻¹, zbar)` equals `g(q, z)` iff `zbar = z − h`.\n\nFrom `g_bar_defect_mul`: the cleared defect is `2q·(zbar − (z−h))`, which\nvanishes exactly when `zbar = z − h`, given `q ≠ 0` and `2 ≠ 0`. No ordering is\nused anywhere — an earlier attempt reached for `nlinarith` and then `linarith`,\nboth of which need an ORDERED field and are simply unavailable over a generic\none. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DecayFibreBarParity.g_bar_defect_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayFibreBarParity.g_bar_defect_mul","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayFibreBarParity.lean#L93-L99","doc":"**The bar-defect of the carrier scalar, cleared of denominators.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DecayFibreBarParity.g_at_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayFibreBarParity.g_at_inv","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayFibreBarParity.lean#L77-L90","doc":"**`g` at the bar point, over the SAME denominator.** `g(q⁻¹, w)` has\ndenominator `q⁻²+1`; clearing it to `q²+1` first is what lets every identity\nbelow close by `ring`. Without this, `field_simp` strands a `(1+q²)⁻¹` inside a\nsum where `ring` cannot reach it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DecayFibreBarParity.chi3S_bar_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayFibreBarParity.chi3S_bar_odd","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayFibreBarParity.lean#L70-L74","doc":"**The fixed character is bar-ODD.** `χ^(3)(Δ_S)` at `q⁻¹` is its negative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DecayFibreBarParity.FullBar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayFibreBarParity.FullBar","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayFibreBarParity.lean#L62-L63","doc":"The full-bar condition on the Markov parameter: `bar(z) = z − h`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DecayFibreBarParity.chi3S","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayFibreBarParity.chi3S","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayFibreBarParity.lean#L59-L60","doc":"`χ^(3)(Δ_S) = h²/2 − h·q`, from `DecayBlockCarrier.chi3_deltaS`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DecayFibreBarParity.g","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayFibreBarParity.g","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayFibreBarParity.lean#L55-L57","doc":"The decay carrier scalar `g(z) = y_(3)(z) − y_(1³)(z)`, from\n`DecayBlockCarrier`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DecayFibreBarParity.hq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayFibreBarParity.hq","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayFibreBarParity.lean#L52-L53","doc":"`h = q − q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}